+    // Papo start - zero-copy outbound framing
+    // When the incoming buffer identity-matches the headroom marker (published by PacketEncoder or
+    // CompressionEncoder earlier in this same write traversal), the frame-length varint is written
+    // right-aligned into the reserved prefix space and the buffer is passed through unmodified - no
+    // output allocation and no payload copy. Any other buffer falls back to the copy-based encode
+    // below. Reference counting: on the fast path the message is transferred with ctx.write (netty
+    // releases it on a synchronous downstream failure); the too-large branch releases it explicitly,
+    // mirroring MessageToByteEncoder's release-on-encode-failure semantics.
+    @Override
